{
  "wire": "low-relay GET /presence, v2: the hub's null is an answer, a fault names its hop (message box #20)",
  "why": [
    "The same agreement as presence-wire-v1.json (kept beside this file as the record of v1):",
    "the relay (handle_presence_route / presence_route_response) PRODUCES these bytes and the",
    "LOW client CONSUMES them; each repo drives its real code through every case and pins the",
    "sha256 of this file's bytes.",
    "",
    "What moved from v1. (1) `present` is true, false or null on a 200. null is the owner hub's",
    "own verdict, 'undecided': a room inside its departure debounce, or a room the hub holds no",
    "sign of (a host who has not joined yet). In v1 the relay folded that null into the 503,",
    "which made every probe of a just-posted lobby room a fault. A client reads null as",
    "unknown, never as away. (2) false may carry lastSeenMs: the hub ends an unmarked empty room",
    "once its last lease or close is older than the idle window (ten minutes), so a client can",
    "age the absence. (3) A 503 ERR_PRESENCE_UNAVAILABLE names the hop that failed (`hop`, and",
    "`hubStatus` on the status hop) and carries the header Retry-After: 5 (`retryAfter` below,",
    "null where the answer carries none). It still has no `present` key.",
    "",
    "`presenceWire` rides the 200 only. A client accepts 1 and 2: a v1 relay's boolean answers",
    "are read as before (the `v1-relay-absence` case), an unmarked false stays unknown to the",
    "host liveness reader (`legacy-absence-no-marker`)."
  ],
  "sha256Note": "The sha256 pinned in both repos is over the exact bytes of this file (including the trailing newline).",
